From 1bb08e968dfd92947040e70a8bedbcb4bc06a3c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:29:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/57] Z 6III: the JPEG cores decode -- playback's and the
 menus' pictures, z63-jpeg-decode

Playback (PLAY) and Setup > monitor colour balance stopped at once on
  Z63_UNMAPPED write addr=0x015e21000 size=4 value=0x39 pc=0x040c0d4c4
the decode job (sub_40C9B4CC) putting a JPEG core in decode mode:
sub_40C0D4B8 writes mode 0x39 -- bit 3 decode, bits 0..2 the 4:2:2 the
encoder takes as 0x31 -- the input (+0x440 << 4; +0x458 its length in
512-byte blocks, 0 for playback: to the EOI), the scale steps (+0x400/
+0x404 bits 2..3) and the output planes (+0x430/+0x434 << 4), and
sub_40C0D614 starts it (+0x004 |= 1, +0x404 = 0x4000). ../z9-qemu's
JPEG model only encodes, and its configuration model refuses the mode.

The handler sub_40C0C774 takes a decoding core through two stops: the
header (status 0x08000000|0x02000000), where it reads the size (+0x1c,
and +0x3c or +0x18), checks the stream's sampling in +0x000 bits 0..2,
programs the output (pitches +0x410/+0x414, size +0x418/+0x41c, a source
window +0x420..+0x428), starts the output DMA (+0x400 = 0x4000) and,
while +0x038 is non-zero, continues the core (+0x004 |= 2); and the end,
as the encoder's (0x0800c000 with +0x02c bit 31), whose 0x60001 the
job's callback sub_40C9BADC takes as done, with the size the header left
in the job.

New z9-capture switch z63-jpeg-decode (on in the board's default props):
a core written a mode with bit 3 belongs to the decode model until a
mode without it. It decodes the stream as it is in RAM with libjpeg
(hw/arm/nikon-z63-jpegdec.h) and gives the handler both stops, writing
NV16 (NV12 for a 4:2:0 stream) into the planes the handler programmed.
DECLARED: both stops immediate; the header stop also sets status bit 12,
which +0x484 enables and the handler ignores in decode mode, so that the
line rises; +0x038 reads 1 between the stops, +0x030/+0x034 read 0; a
stream libjpeg refuses ends in status 0x20400000, which the handler
takes as an error.

Checked: PLAY decodes the newest picture's 1620x1080 preview (JPEG_1,
y=0xa3769d380 pitch 1632); monitor colour balance opens and decodes the
same, no stop (its picture area stays black: it is drawn by a YUV path
the GFX model skips). Releases still write DSC_nnnn.JPG.

Playback now stops one step later, where the resizer scales the decoded
picture from RAM: A1 (0x15421100) +4 = 0x5001, pc 0x40c27448, with the
coefficient banks 0x15427000/0x15428000 and output instance 0x15432000.
../z9-qemu models RAM input only for the thumbnail route (A2 -> F4 ->
B4). That route is the next step for playback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
